ing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $31K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $17K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Chewy, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $9.1B market cap on $12.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Gross margins of 28% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The business throws off $562M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.10\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -13.9% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 55\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 2.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.7% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 81% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8095402825821661},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Chewy (CHWY) Adds Spirited Paw As Fair Value Narrative Faces A Fresh Test","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/retail/nyse-chwy/chewy/news/chewy-chwy-adds-spirited-paw-as-fair-value-narrative-faces-a","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793943079.763,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.957,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Chewy (CHWY) Stock Moves -1.71%: What You Should Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024944/chewy-chwy-stock-moves-1-71-what-you-should-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_6-3024944","date":"2026